    "title": "Former Steelers QB Russell Wilson gets offer from New York Jets - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Curt Popejoy ,\n5 hours ago Jan 11, 2025; Baltimore, Maryland, USA; Pittsburgh Steelers quarterback Russell Wilson (3) looks to pass against Baltimore Ravens linebacker Tavius Robinson (95) in the third quarter in an AFC wild card game at M&T Bank Stadium. Mandatory Credit: Tommy Gilligan-Imagn Images By Tommy Gilligan, Tommy Gilligan-Imagn Images In 2024, quarterback Russell Wilson was supposed to be the answer for the Pittsburgh Steelers . But a training camp calf injury from pushing a blocking sled cost Wilson nearly half the season and once he got on the field he started fast and then sputtered down the stretch.\nWilson then signed with the New York Giants in 2025 but went 0-3 as a starter while backing up Jaxson Dart. Now, according to the New York Post, via Dov Kleiman, the New York Jets have offered Wilson a contract where he would compete with Geno Smith for the starting quarterback spot.\nMeanwhile, the Steelers continue to sit and wait for veteran Aaron Rodgers to decide if he wants to run it back for another season in Pittsburgh.\nThis article originally appeared on Steelers Wire: Former Steelers QB Russell Wilson gets offer from New York Jets\n2",
    "summary": "5 hours ago Jan 11, 2025; Baltimore, Maryland, USA; Pittsburgh Steelers quarterback Russell Wilson (3) looks to pass against Baltimore Ravens linebacker Tavius Robinson (95) in the third quarter in an AFC wild card game at M&T Bank Stadium. But a training camp calf injury from pushing a blocking sled cost Wilson nearly half the season and once he got on the field he started fast and then sputtered down the stretch. Wilson then signed with the New York Giants in 2025 but went 0-3 as a starter while backing up Jaxson Dart.",
